# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration Report

## Summary
Updated the Vercel Web Analytics integration to use the latest recommended import for Next.js App Router projects.

## What Was Changed

### Modified Files:
- **src/app/layout.tsx** - Updated Analytics import path

## Changes Made

### Before:
```typescript
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";
```

### After:
```typescript
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";
```

## Rationale

According to the official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), for Next.js App Router projects, the Analytics component should be imported from `@vercel/analytics/next` instead of `@vercel/analytics/react`. 

The `/next` import is specifically optimized for Next.js and provides better integration with Next.js features like Server Components and the App Router.

## Verification Steps Completed

1. ✅ Verified `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) is already installed
2. ✅ Updated import statement to use the Next.js-specific path
3. ✅ Built the project successfully with `npm run build`
4. ✅ Ran linter with `npm run lint` - no errors
5. ✅ Ran complete test suite - all 103 tests passed (100%)

## Technical Notes

- The `<Analytics />` component placement in the layout is correct (at the end of the `<body>` tag)
- No additional configuration or environment variables are required
- The package was already installed, so no dependency changes were needed
- The Analytics component will automatically track page views and user interactions once deployed to Vercel

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Visit the deployed site to generate some traffic
3. Check the Vercel Analytics dashboard to verify data collection is working
4. Optionally configure custom events for specific user interactions (Pro/Enterprise plans)
